WEBVTT

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.190
Thanks to you,

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:39.200
all of Mealtars' people were
able to escape unharmed.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.080
I would like to express my gratitude
to you both on their behalf.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:48.340
Helping the oppressed is the
greatest wish of the Teachings of Levetia.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:52.260
We are delighted we could
save them from the empire's tyranny.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.970
How did you end up as
Mealtars' representative?

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.890
That is a rather long
and complicated story.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.020
But this gentleman is their mayor,
and I have his consent.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.360
If I may, I have a question for you.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.900
Your army so graciously defended us,
but what will they do now?

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.410
Is it not obvious? They will drive back
the princes' armies and free the city.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.030
Is that not right, King Gruyere?

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.450
Yes, that was the plan.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.500
We cannot thank you enough.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.630
We escaped the city unharmed
thanks to the threat of your host.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.340
But to fall further into your debt
could only be deemed ungracious of us.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.720
What would you do if you removed
yourselves from our protection?

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.140
We will reclaim the city by our own hand.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.060
To that end, we would like to purchase
your army's excess weapons and food.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.770
We'll pay triple the going price.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.650
Now, let's see what they say.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.410
You wish to buy our excess supplies?

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.090
Of course, I am well aware that
you act according to God's divine will.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.960
As such, your holy army will not
be swayed by money.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.760
However, Mealtars is a mercantile city,

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.640
and coin is the traditional
symbol of good faith.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.520
Please allow us to pay you.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.430
Once we retake the city,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.270
we shall erect a monument
and temple in praise of your deeds.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.900
Now that the Levetians have
30,000 refugees under their wing,

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.410
their options must be limited.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:08.830
I imagine they'd like
to return home at once, but...

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.410
You are offering us coin and renown

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.460
if we leave you weapons
and food and return home?

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.210
He is a marvel. He truly is.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.550
That move was far beyond
all my expectations.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.380
So, Prince Wein,

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:28.560
I must refuse you for that very reason.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.730
How delightful. I'd love to play
with this boy some more.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.440
I would deny him, frustrate him,
and then poke and prod the wound.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.320
I want to see how
he reacts after that and--

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.400
We accept.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.610
What?

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:45.570
King Gruyere, what did you just say?

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:50.540
I said I accept his proposal, Caldmellia,
Director of the Bureau of Teachings.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:54.000
Am I not the one responsible
for this decision?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.960
I have the military under my charge.
As such, I say this:

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.380
We should accept his proposal.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.550
He will likely create a militia
from the people of Mealtars.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.010
Once the imperial princes
are worn down by battle,

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.600
he'll urge them to negotiate.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.230
We could press the matter and
have Mealtars fight alongside us,

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:19.480
but I have no intention of getting
caught up in your capricious actions.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.320
We will only sell our surplus supplies.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.700
Our army stays put until we confirm
that your people have retaken the city.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.490
I've no objections.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:32.870
I thank you from the bottom of
my heart for your cooperation.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.330
I have a report for His Highness!

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.040
What?! The people of Mealtars
have taken up arms?!

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.380
Yes, Your Highness! They're armed
and are coming down the hill!

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.260
The people have been
organized into a militia,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.970
but can they repel my brothers' armies?

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:53.680
The princes see Mealtars' people
as the goose that lays golden eggs.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.560
They won't want to fight because
the more they kill, the less they profit.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:03.150
Plus, the Levetian army is
still unscathed and in reserve.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.110
Send a message to Manfred at once!

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.910
Now for the final touch.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.990
Lowa, ask the princes
to gather for a meeting.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.740
Wait, not that trick?

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.870
Yep, it's the go-to move
at times like these!

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:24.630
You know who's behind
the assassination attempt?!

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.550
Yes.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:30.470
Don't tell me you're
accusing Bardloche and me?

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.760
I couldn't stop thinking about it.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.890
Why would the assassin do such a thing?

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.690
Care to explain?

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:41.600
Security in the city was airtight.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:45.230
Plus, private guards were
placed at each compound.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:49.240
It's hard to believe an assassin could
succeed under such circumstances.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.780
But there is one likely suspect.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:57.410
It's neither me nor
anyone else in this room.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:58.620
Don't tell me...

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.340
That's right! This was all
the work of Prince Demetrio!

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.510
That is the truth behind this crime.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:10.470
That's absurd!
Why would he do such a thing?!

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:13.800
Mealtars' standing suffered
when it fell under suspicion,

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.600
and both of your forces
were weakened in the fighting.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.810
If he were to return and attack you,

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.980
he could claim Mealtars and the throne.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.820
Then Prince Demetrio would be victorious.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:32.030
I have no doubt that Demetrio never
intended for the summit to succeed.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:34.740
That's why he was not
receptive to our discussions

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.290
and kept pressing his claim to the throne.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.250
Don't tell me it's all...

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.170
...getting pinned on Demetrio.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:48.510
That's right. The failed summit,
the assassination attempt,

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:52.130
the war, the bad weather tomorrow,
and everything under the sun!

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:54.590
We'll pin it all on Demetrio!

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:58.100
And there it is.
Wein's patented trial in absentia.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.850
Mealtars knows this was not
a fight either of you sought.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:05.650
As such, we are prepared
to pay sufficient compensation.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:11.860
And we shall refrain from pursuing any
future relations with Prince Demetrio.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:16.280
If I reject their proposal,
Manfred will likely agree to it.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.950
If I reject their proposal and
Bardloche and I take Mealtars,

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:23.040
we'll still end up
fighting over the throne.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.790
That will only end up
benefitting Demetrio.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.960
He alone will claim victory.

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:30.550
Very well, then.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.340
I agree to your proposal.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:36.430
I knew you two would be on board!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:42.600
I am afraid we have caused you
much needless trouble.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.060
Think nothing of it.

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:49.400
It was a wonderful opportunity
to build strong ties with Mealtars.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:53.150
Pinning the blame on Demetrio
will take the wind out of his sails.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:56.780
The same goes for my brothers'
forces surrounding the city.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.240
As a result,

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.450
Mealtars is now firmly
ensconced in my faction.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:09.210
Of course, I am well aware that the hearts
of your people lie with you, not me.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.170
This has made me realize something.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:17.640
The measure of a sovereign
is more than just strength.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:23.480
I asked Prince Wein a question before
our talks with King Gruyere and company.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:28.190
I said, "Why have you been so eager
to work together with Mealtars?"

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:30.020
What did he say?

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:33.230
Falanya has taken a shine to your city.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:38.110
What big brother wouldn't want his
little sister to return home triumphant.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:44.120
To think it was all to gladden
the heart of his little sister.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:48.880
I'm amazed he would wager his
fate along with our city's just for that.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:00.100
Sheesh. I guess I'm not
used to laughing that hard.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.300
Let's try that a--

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.640
Enough already.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:06.060
What's the point of straining
your voice for something so dumb?

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.600
Chances like this don't come too often.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:11.770
I don't see anything wrong
with enjoying the moment.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.030
Well, I do understand how you feel.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:18.320
I never expected our exports to be such
a success and fuel a booming economy.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:22.620
If we continue to prosper, the people
will rejoice, and our budget will grow.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.620
We'll have more options,
and the kingdom's value will rise.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.000
Talk about too much of a good thing!

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.380
I see a cushy life ahead
in my princely future!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.670
Wasn't long ago you were carrying on about
retiring and selling off the kingdom.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:40.300
Retire? Sell off the kingdom?
I don't know <i>what </i>you're talking about!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.220
I'll indulge in every possible luxury

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:46.060
while milking my current
position for as long as I can!

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.350
I'm impressed by how far revenue
from the Marden region has grown.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.860
I know! It's all thanks to my bright idea!

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:53.520
"Marden"    "Natra"

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:53.520
I know! It's all thanks to my bright idea!

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:54.270
"Marden"    "Natra"

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:54.270
By swearing allegiance to Natra,

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.650
"Natra"
"Mardenian region"

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.650
By swearing allegiance to Natra,

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:59.740
"Earthwold Empire"

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:59.740
Marden now has access to an
abundance of goods from the east.

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:04.240
But the nations of the west won't
welcome such commerce with open arms.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:09.660
The Levetians view the continent's
eastern half as barbarian territory.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.420
They're even prejudiced
against the east's goods.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:16.460
That's why I've conspired with Marden
to falsify the land of origin.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:19.970
We're exporting the empire's
products as if they were Natra's!

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.380
It's a revolutionary idea!

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.640
The venture has been a jackpot,

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:27.060
greatly enriching Marden's coffers.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:31.390
It's tough being such
a genius. It really is!

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.690
But if this keeps up,

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.900
Marden's economy will
rival ours in less than ten years.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.780
Worst case, they'll declare independence.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.530
We can't let <i>that </i>happen.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:46.450
We need to find another
major trading partner.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.910
Enter.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.960
Excuse me, Highness.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.380
An envoy has just arrived
from the Kingdom of Soljest.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.500
From Soljest?

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.800
I'll be right there.
Show them to the audience chamber.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.880
Highness!

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:08.100
Soljest? What do you suppose
King Gruyere wants?

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.520
I just thought of a great plan.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:17.820
Prince Wein is to visit Marden?

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:22.950
Yes, it seems His Highness was invited
to a ceremony in the Kingdom of Soljest

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.660
and would like to
visit our land on his way.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:29.740
The prince is no doubt concerned
about the future of Marden

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.790
as a vassal state of Natra.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:36.840
Understood. Let us put His Highness's
mind to rest by showing our allegiance.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:40.010
Yes, but Marden is now
in a prime position.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:43.680
This is a chance to redress
the disparities in our relationship.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:47.550
We may even be able
to extract some concessions.

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:53.440
Tell me, Jiva, what sort of concessions
do you think we should extract?

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:58.860
Marriage between you, Lady Zenovia,
and His Highness, Prince Wein.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:04.030
With negotiations in Soljest near at hand,
he'll no doubt avoid a clear answer.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:09.030
But it would be in our best interests to
extract a commitment while he is here.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:13.000
If such a marriage comes to pass,
it will boost Marden's standing in Natra

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.040
and greatly expand our influence.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:19.170
But only if I can become his bride.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.470
Does it bother you that much?

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.050
I'd like to muss it up, to say the least.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:32.310
No, the color will come off.
I already told you.

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.140
What about my princely prerogative?

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.310
No means no.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:40.770
So, about what you said.
Do you really intend to wed Zenovia?

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:44.740
As if. I'd like to stay single for now.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:45.820
Why?

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:51.450
I want to enjoy having all sorts of ladies
begging for my hand in marriage.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.160
I was joking!

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.950
Don't worry. I won't break it.

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:58.710
The title of queen consort
is a useful negotiating tool

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:00.000
--if we keep it up for grabs.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.920
--That's true.
--if we keep it up for grabs.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.260
So, the purpose of this visit

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:09.800
is to see whether Marden intends to
adopt a cooperative attitude toward Natra.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.600
And if they are cooperative,

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.180
they're almost guaranteed
to demand that I wed Zenovia.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:18.400
In turn, I will do everything
to evade the issue.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.230
You are just plain awful.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.980
I bid you welcome.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:28.070
You are too gracious, Marchioness Zenovia.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.450
Your Highness, there is
no need to stand on ceremony.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.740
Zenovia alone will suffice.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:37.290
Then with your permission, Zeno...

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.580
...via.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.710
Boobies!

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:44.300
No, you idiot!
Focus with all your strength!

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:49.680
I was shocked the first time
I heard about it.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:54.350
To think you would import imperial goods
and market them as Natran made.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:58.810
It was all for the benefit of the good
and godly people of the west.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.270
I simply got a bit creative.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:05.110
Zenovia, rapid growth may
sometimes be a source of stress.

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:09.240
I would be happy to discuss
any concerns you might have.

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:12.410
Well, since you mentioned it,

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:16.870
the Kingdom of Delunio sent a letter
of protest regarding trade goods.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.250
From Delunio?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:22.000
So Marden also received that letter.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.630
So you did, too?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.710
Yes, it was a complaint
about our trade goods.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.630
Their kingdom is extremely conservative.

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.800
And their king is quite young,

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:37.470
so most political matters are handled
by their prime minister, Sirgis.

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:42.270
He is quite patriotic and a fervent
follower of the Teachings of Levetia.

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:47.650
He seeks to preserve his kingdom's culture
while casting out foreign influences.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.530
As such, he likely
harbors resentment toward us.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:54.030
Keep the goods flowing.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.660
Are you sure?

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:59.250
He can't be <i>that </i>serious
if he merely sent a letter.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.870
Don't take him seriously

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:04.790
until there is a line of envoys
protesting outside your door.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.880
All right, I will do that.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.680
Wait. Is that all she has to say?

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.060
When I asked if she had any concerns,

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:22.310
I thought she'd mention the disparities
in our kingdom and bring up our marriage.

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:25.230
That's what I was banking on, at least.

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:32.400
You were so sure
she'd ask you to marry her.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:35.240
Then you were supposed
to coolly brush her off.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.750
She'll have to make some
kind of move tomorrow!

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.960
I bet she'll drop a hint
during the tour of the city!

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:49.170
Let's hope they don't think
you suffer from an inflated ego.

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:53.760
That's the one thing I want
to avoid for the sake of my honor!

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:01.850
I am honored to see you again,
Your Highness.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.360
Zeno, may I ask how
you serve the marchioness?

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:09.940
I am one of Lady Zenovia's attendants.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:13.450
I watch over the city and handle
other affairs in milady's stead.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:17.780
Today, she asked me to tell you
to please enjoy the tour of our city.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:22.250
I bet she'll try to break the ice
while she shows me around.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.960
Now then, shall we begin?

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:37.140
The bronze statues in our central plaza

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:41.430
were erected as a symbol of Marden's
desire for peace and prosperity.

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:45.850
Our land has yet to fully heal
from the recent war.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:49.940
But all of us hope that we have
finally achieved a lasting peace.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.190
Have no fear.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:55.820
Marden will continue to thrive
as long as the economy is booming.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:18:00.490
Economic power means you can
ward off outside interference.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:05.080
And as you grow strong, you can join
your neighbors in a bid for independence.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.540
Is that not an eventual
option open to you?

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:10.460
Surely you jest?

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:15.170
Lady Zenovia and her vassals
are happy to be a part of Natra.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:19.140
We believe that is the best way
to assure Marden's prosperity.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:20.350
I see.

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:24.890
So she intends to maintain a
cooperative relationship with Natra.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.140
In that case...

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:29.730
Shall we take a break?
There is a bench over there.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:34.230
Here it comes! She's going
to broach the subject of marriage!

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.280
What do you think of our city?

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.660
The sights were magnificent,
as is the energy of your people.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:45.620
Seeing it firsthand made me realize
how much they are counting on you.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:50.460
Indeed. My support continues
to grow as the economy booms.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:54.300
A good relationship between rulers
and their people never hurts.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.300
But you can never rest easy.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:00.550
I have always wanted to ask you.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:05.140
Why is Your Highness
so wary of the people?

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.060
Wary?

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:10.520
Well, maybe wary isn't
really the right word.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.810
Perhaps "oddly distant" is better.

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.900
Well...

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:17.110
...let me ask you this.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:19.400
Are noble and royal bloodlines venerable?

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:21.910
What? Of course they are!

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:25.540
Everyone believes that they are.

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:28.000
Then let me ask you this.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:32.040
At what point do you think
they became venerable?

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:35.420
I'm not sure I follow.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:38.090
For instance, I am a member
of the Natran royal family.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:43.010
If noble and royal bloodlines are
venerable, when did I become so?

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.510
When you were born?

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:47.810
Right.

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:52.730
Those born of a venerable bloodline
will also be of venerable blood.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:55.150
So then, when did
my father become venerable?

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:58.360
When he was born, of course,
just like Your Highness.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:19:59.570
Exactly.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:03.320
Children born of royalty are venerable
because their parents are, too.

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:06.620
And <i>their </i>parents, too, are venerable,
and so on down the line.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.410
It's simple logic.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.040
So then, Ninym.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:14.290
If we traced my bloodline back through
history, where would we end up?

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:19.010
Caleus, a chief disciple of Levetia,
founder of the Levetian religion.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.590
Right.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:25.100
However, he was but a humble farmer
until Levetia found him.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.010
His parents were, too.

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:29.350
So back to that question.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:33.650
At what point did Caleus's
bloodline become venerable?

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:39.070
Once he started following Levetia
and accomplished many great deeds?

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.110
Precisely.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:45.910
By virtue of their brains,
their brawn, or even plain luck,

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:49.240
commoners can distinguish
themselves and gain renown.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:52.160
If you trace back through
all venerable bloodlines,

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:54.420
you'll always end up at a commoner.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:58.340
What does that have
to do with my question?

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:02.170
In short, all nobility and royalty,
even the most haughty,

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:04.590
were commoners
if you trace all the way back.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:07.850
That means even those despised
as commoners today

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:11.220
can become nobles or even royalty one day.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:24.030
Now back to your first question.
Why am I wary of the people?

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:27.160
Natra is home to some 800,000 people.

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:33.710
There are that many nameless yet
potential royals watching my every move.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:36.580
How could I live like
that without being wary?

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:41.130
I suppose that's why many royals

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:45.510
try to create mythologies
surrounding their families.

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.090
What's the matter?

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:53.220
Nothing really. It's just, I am once again
overwhelmed by how great a man you are.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.980
Pay it no mind.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.850
A great man?

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:59.190
I'm glad you think so,

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:03.150
but I'm not feeling
very great at the moment.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:04.070
Why is that?

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:08.910
Truth be told, a wedding proposal
I'd expected never materialized.

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:13.370
And so I started to think
that maybe I had an inflated ego.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:18.120
I know not whom you speak of.

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:23.880
But if it is a certain Mardenian,
she is too busy with the affairs of state.

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.840
I believe marriage would be unthinkable.

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:30.970
B-But if she married me, those affairs
that make her busy would vanish.

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:33.010
Wouldn't that be handy?

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:39.350
While that may be true,
she may also have a shallower reason.

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:41.110
A shallower reason?

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:46.900
For instance, Your Highness's face
is not her type. Things like that.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:52.080
No, that was simply a jest.

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:57.460
W-Well, it's about time we get back.
Let us return to the palace.

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:02.040
The light at this time of day gives
a whole different look to the city.

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:06.010
My face isn't her type.

00:23:06.010 --> 00:23:09.470
Stupid inflated ego!

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:14.810
Let it go, already. It was
spur-of-the-moment subterfuge.

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:17.390
I'm entering hibernation. See you later.

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:19.230
You're impossible.

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:20.940
Forgive me, Jiva.

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:25.150
I disregarded your idea of marriage.

00:23:25.150 --> 00:23:29.860
The prince seems distant and a bit scary.

00:23:29.860 --> 00:23:35.080
So then Prince Wein is like a
sort of hero to you, Lady Zenovia.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:38.500
Yes, that is painfully apparent
when I speak with him.

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:43.460
And it reminds me that I could
never be queen to such a great man.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:47.800
I know that such a marriage
would be a clever move.

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:50.220
Passing it up means I failed as a leader.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:54.930
You need not wed His Highness
if your heart is in doubt.

00:23:54.930 --> 00:23:59.890
Take comfort in knowing your vassals
shall help you find the best way forward.

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:01.190
Thank you.

00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:02.900
It is our duty.

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:03.940
Milady!

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:05.190
What is it?!

00:24:05.190 --> 00:24:08.570
Delunio's prime minister
is at the front gate!

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:10.400
Sirgis is here?!
